# Try an image effect
@scenario office_lesson_18
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg office]
[char pip global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show pip desk point]
pip: An image effect can make a drawing quiver. Compare the still and treated versions.
[if !tutorial_still]
[set character.pip.imageEffect pikupiku.lineboil]
[endif]
pip: Hold this frame for a moment.
[set character.pip.imageEffect none]
pip: Edit the optional image-effect ID below. Set it back to none when you finish comparing.
@label check
pip: What is the clean baseline for judging a sprite effect?
> A different pose and new lighting. -> retry
> The same pose with its effect off. -> correct
@label retry
[show pip desk curious]
pip: Keeping the input fixed isolates the change the effect makes. Give it another try.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show pip desk cheer]
pip: Keeping the input fixed isolates the change the effect makes.
> Finish this lesson -> return_hub
> Try the lesson again -> start
@label return_hub
[if !tutorial_done_18]
[flag tutorial_done_18]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_4]
